A||||4||PlasticWrapd||Running rich again... back to the drawing board...||||8||
Z||000000||PlasticWrapd||12-07-2000||02:58 AM||||Well, here I am again, stumped!  Here's the problem...<P>1984 2.5 w/M19.  Engine runs RICH!  I mean the exhaust is rich enough to burn your eyes and throat if you get too close.  <P>New o2 sensor, injector seems okay, no drips or leaks, decent spray pattern.  No codes in the computer, other than a 44 (lean exhaust)but only once.  Car gets 15-18 mpg from a 4 banger!  <P>Very small coolant leak where intake bolts to head right next to #4 intake port.  Head gasket seems okay (cooling system is not immediately pressurized when engine starts) no water in oil or vice versa.  What happens if the coolant is getting into the #4 intake port?  Fool the o2 sensor into reading a lean condition causing the injector to fire at a higher frequency?<P>Has a problem with the starter not working all the time.  +13v on purple wire (connects to solenoid coil) when key is turned to start position and clutch is floored.  Seems like a grounding problem.  Poor ground cause the rich condition?<P>Help!!!  Getting to the point of throwing tools across the garage!<P>||||reg||8
Z||000001||strdream||12-07-2000||09:31 AM||||Yes poor grounds and electrical connections are a common problem.  Coolant can coat the ox. sensor and screw it up.  If the engine is misfireing there is un-spent oxygen going out the exhaust,  the o2 sensor will see that and give it a false lean reading.<P>13v on that wire under laod does not alarm me.  It's probably time to replace the starter and solinoid. <P>keep digging, Be patient,  flying wrenchs are never solve problems unless they happen to hit a ****  roach or somthing.<P>Ross <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||12-07-2000||09:42 AM||||Check your timming and insure that it is correct. The coolant leak at #4, is it on the outboard (drivers side) of the manifold? Water in the combustion chamber will make steam vapor whenever engine is running.<BR>If you have a high milage car with the factory exhaust still intact, replace or remove the converter as when they start to go bad a common symptom is a 'burning in the eyes' sensation.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-07-2000||10:55 PM||||If coolant is getting dumped into the intake it will usually ruin the O2. <P>Coolant leaking at the intake could be the passage that runs under the TBI to heat the bottom of the manifold. You need to get that fixed and then work thru the rest of it. You'll have to replace the intake manifold gasket.||||reg||1
Z||000004||WisconsinGT||12-08-2000||09:13 AM||||Plastic, Try and do a compression test. If a cyl. is low, that could be your problem. FWIW||||reg||1
